# Test: fib-vpp plugin auto-loads, and refuses to program routes when the
#       VPP subsystem is present but disabled.
#
# VALIDATES: fib-vpp is wired into the config-driven auto-load pipeline
#            (ConfigRoots: ["fib.vpp"]); OnStarted subscribes to
#            (system-rib, best-change) and, with GetActiveConnector() nil,
#            refuses to build a writer (openFibVPPWriter) and logs why.
# PREVENTS:  fib-vpp becoming library-only dead code (the "feature not
#            wired" mistake from memory), and the silent noop backend this
#            test once required: a writer with no VPP behind it reported
#            every route as installed while VPP held none. If the
#            ConfigRoot changes, the auto-loader path breaks, or the noop
#            fallback returns, this test catches it.
#
# Method: spawn ze with a minimal bgp + fib.vpp config; assert the
# plugin's refusal log line appears on stderr within the timeout, and that
# neither the noop fallback line nor the writer loop's "running" line does.
# Uses the same bounded child-process orchestration as the other compiled
# standalone lifecycle drivers.
#
# The vpp subsystem loads (its config block is present) but stays inert
# because vpp.enabled is false; GetActiveConnector() therefore returns
# nil and fib-vpp logs the refusal naming the cause and 'ze doctor'.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/fib-vpp-plugin-load:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=fib-vpp: no route is programmed into VPP
expect=stderr:pattern=the vpp component is not running
reject=stderr:pattern=using noop backend
reject=stderr:pattern=fib-vpp: running
